{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And this shall be peace</b> — no man shall fear Assyria if he comes into our land. Furthermore: <b>they shall raise against him</b> — the meaning is, if Assyria wishes to come into our land, the officers of this ruler shall raise up many." "<b>Seven</b> — also eight, in the manner of: 'give a portion to seven and also to eight.' The meaning is doubled, for princes are like shepherds, and note: it is not fifteen."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:56.417480310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}